# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All values here are OPTIONAL. The portfolio builds and runs with none of them.
#
# They are commented out on purpose. Some hosts (Vercel's import flow among
# them) read this file and pre-create every key they find, with an empty value
# — and an empty value is not the same as an unset one. The site now treats
# blank and malformed values as unset, but leaving these commented keeps the
# host's environment clean in the first place.
#
# To use one locally: copy this file to `.env.local` and uncomment the line.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored — never commit real secrets.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Canonical production URL, used for SEO metadata, sitemap.xml and robots.txt.
# Set this once you have a custom domain. A missing https:// is added for you.
#
# On Vercel you do not need to set this at all — the site reads Vercel's own
# production domain automatically. On GitHub Pages the deploy workflow sets it.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://chandrasekhar.dev

# Sub-path the site is served from. Leave unset for Vercel / Netlify / a custom
# domain, all of which serve from the root. The GitHub Pages workflow sets this
# automatically to "/<repo-name>".
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/chandrasekhar-portfolio
